The '''Union del Personajes''' was an anti-[[Volisania]], pro-worker political current in mid-nineteenth-century Sarta. It drew support from miners, rural communities, and inland districts that had borne the costs of industrial growth without receiving equal benefits.

The union argued for stronger labour protections, tighter regulation of the royal companies, and a more independent Sartan foreign policy. It was strongest outside the capital and coastal commercial zones, especially in the rural south, the mining districts, and the mountainous interior.

== Political position ==

The Union del Personajes treated the mining stoppages and rural unrest of the 1850s as evidence that Sarta needed a political order less dependent on Volisanian trade and less controlled by business elites. It opposed the pro-business Liga Progressivo on questions of labour, company oversight, and foreign alignment.

The union became one of the two main political divisions of the era and gave a parliamentary voice to workers and inland reformers after the creation of the [[House of Commons of Sarta]].

== Base of support ==

Its support was strongest among mine workers, rural Petran communities, and inland towns that had sent migrants to the coast. It also drew backing from reformers who wanted the lower house to become a genuine counterweight to the lords.

